    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d459">

                <pb facs="0641" n="551" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg551"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/1857: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-18T20:00:00+08:00">April 18, 1934—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 18—12:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>181. Following is paraphrase of message received from Peck at Nanking in comment
                    on his April 18, 10 a.m., to the Department concerning claims commission: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The action reported in my April 18, 10 a.m., was apparently not
                            contemplated by the Foreign Office when it drafted <hi
                                rendition="#italic">note verbale</hi> of April 16th.<anchor n="5"
                                xml:id="d459-f1"/> I am inclined to interpret this partial
                            concession as a diplomatic gesture, confirmation of Sino-Japanese crisis
                            reported in my April 18, 9 a.m.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d459-f2"/></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Note verbale</hi> of April 16th was an unsatisfactory
                    reply to Legation’s recent note on claims commission. It requested list of
                    debtors.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d459-f1" n="5" xml:id="d459-f1-content">
